, then move to one <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/backend-languages\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">back-end language<\/a> and a database. Build three or four projects, put them on GitHub, and apply for internships to gain real work experience.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-full-stack-developer\/#faq-question-1786361469250","position":3,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-full-stack-developer\/#faq-question-1786361469250","name":"3. How long does it take to become a Full Stack Developer?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most learners need 6 to 12 months to build solid foundational skills with regular practice. Reaching a professional level takes another year or two of hands-on\u00a0projects\u00a0and job experience.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-full-stack-developer\/#faq-question-1786361484376","position":4,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-full-stack-developer\/#faq-question-1786361484376","name":"4. Is it difficult to become a Full Stack Developer?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It is not difficult, but it does take time and consistency. Break the learning into small steps,\u00a0practice\u00a0daily, and work on real projects instead of only watching tutorials.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-full-stack-developer\/#faq-question-1786361502876","position":5,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-full-stack-developer\/#faq-question-1786361502876","name":"5. What programming languages should I learn to become a Full Stack Developer?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Start with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript for the front-end, then 